<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    DnnMigration.Infrastructure
    ============================================================================
    SDK-style C# class library for the INFRASTRUCTURE layer of the DNN 4.x -> .NET 8
    Clean/Onion Architecture backend. It houses the EF Core 8 persistence stack
    (Persistence/DnnDbContext + Persistence/Configurations/* IEntityTypeConfiguration
    mappings + Repositories/*) and the identity services that replace the legacy
    Forms-Authentication / DES model (Identity/JwtService, Identity/PasswordHasher).

    Dependency direction (Clean Architecture, inward only):
        Api -> Application -> Domain ;  Infrastructure -> Application -> Domain
    This project IMPLEMENTS the Domain repository interfaces (IPortalRepository,
    IModuleRepository, IUserRepository, IRoleRepository, ITabRepository in
    DnnMigration.Domain.Interfaces) and the Application identity ports (IJwtService,
    IPasswordHasher in DnnMigration.Application.Interfaces). It is referenced by
    DnnMigration.Api (DI composition root) and exercised by
    DnnMigration.IntegrationTests. It must NEVER reference Api (that would invert
    the architecture). Build/declare order: Domain -> Application -> Infrastructure -> Api.

    Shared build configuration is centralized in backend/Directory.Build.props,
    which MSBuild imports automatically by walking up the directory tree. That
    props file is the single source of truth for TargetFramework (net8.0),
    LangVersion (12.0), Nullable, ImplicitUsings, TreatWarningsAsErrors,
    WarningsNotAsErrors (CS8618), Deterministic and GenerateDocumentationFile, so
    none of those settings are repeated here. The output type defaults to a class
    library, and RootNamespace/AssemblyName default from the file name
    'DnnMigration.Infrastructure' (matching DnnMigration.Infrastructure.Persistence /
    .Persistence.Configurations / .Repositories / .Identity), so no PropertyGroup
    or OutputType override is required.

    Package references are limited to what this layer consumes directly:
      * Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer 8.0.11 - EF Core 8 ORM + SQL Server
        (TDS) provider for DnnDbContext and the repositories. It transitively brings
        the base Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore and Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational
        packages (so they are deliberately NOT listed separately) and, through the
        EF Core 8 Microsoft.Extensions.* 8.x closure, Microsoft.Extensions.Options
        (IOptions<JwtSettings>) - also not listed separately.
      * Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design 8.0.11 - design-time support, marked
        PrivateAssets=all so it does not flow transitively to Api or the test projects.
      * Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools 8.0.11 - PMC/CLI tooling, likewise
        PrivateAssets=all. Listed per AAP 0.5.1; harmless under PrivateAssets even
        though ADR-002 forbids EF migrations.
      * BCrypt.Net-Next 4.0.3 - adaptive password hashing in Identity/PasswordHasher.cs
        (replaces the legacy 56-bit DES Encrypt/Decrypt of PortalSecurity.vb).
      * System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt 7.1.2 - JwtSecurityToken(Handler) and
        JwtRegisteredClaimNames for token issuance/validation in Identity/JwtService.cs.
      * Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens 7.1.2 - SymmetricSecurityKey, SigningCredentials,
        SecurityAlgorithms and TokenValidationParameters for Identity/JwtService.cs.
    The two IdentityModel packages are pinned to 7.1.2 to unify the solution-wide
    NuGet graph with DnnMigration.Api's Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer
    8.0.11 (whose 8.0.x line resolves Microsoft.IdentityModel.* >= 7.1.2), so token
    issuance here and validation in the Api pipeline agree on the same assemblies and
    the zero-warning Release build (Gate 1) reports no NU1605/NU1608.

    Structure reference only (NOT a 1:1 port): the legacy VB.NET project
    Library/DotNetNuke.Library.vbproj merely confirms this is a class library. No
    legacy <Import>, Option Strict/Explicit, Microsoft.VisualBasic / SqlHelper /
    System.Web* references, or AssemblyInfo carryover are reproduced here.
    ============================================================================
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DnnMigration.Domain\DnnMigration.Domain.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DnnMigration.Application\DnnMigration.Application.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer" Version="8.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design" Version="8.0.11">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools" Version="8.0.11">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="BCrypt.Net-Next" Version="4.0.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt" Version="7.1.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens" Version="7.1.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
